 "idea": {
  "id": "opex_week",
  "family": "calendar",
  "title": "Hold the index in the week of the monthly option expiry",
  "why": "Stivers and Sun (2013) found large stocks earn most of their return in the week of the third Friday, when dealers unwind the hedges behind expiring options. The following week has tended to be weak. Both are known dates. Tested on the index fund only; no option data is used.",
